{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ctw5kyStEz4f8qmWyRqvkA","type":"tool_result","content":"### What was implemented\r\n- bev-diagnostic-rectification/_reference/hv-component-index.json: 18 HV components with id, name_en, name_bm, function, voltage_range, safety_standard, cus_referenced\r\n- scripts/index_hv_components.py: extract_components(), validate_safety_fields(), scan_kp_files(), build_index(), generate_validation_report() + CLI with --update flag\r\n- tests/test_hv_component_index.py: 19 tests across 5 test classes — all pass\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- importlib module loading pattern: spec_from_file_location + sys.modules registration works cleanly for scripts/ dir\r\n- extract_components() uses lowercase keyword matching dict (component_id -> [keywords]) for deterministic scanning\r\n- validate_safety_fields() returns list of error strings; empty = valid (clean for pytest assertions)\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- _reference/ directory must be created before writing JSON (it didn't exist)\r\n- Windows: all file reads use encoding='utf-8' explicitly\r\n## Iteration 4 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  5:31:13 PM\r\nCompleted: BEV HV System Component Cross-Reference Indexer (ID: US-038) in 5m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  5:45:50 PM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Assessment Question Time-Box Validator (ID: US-039) — 7061 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration 2 - Story: Assessment Question Time-Box Validator (US-039)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- _tools/assessment-time-validator.py: estimate_question_time(), calculate_assessment_duration(), generate_report() — parses all KA/PA files, classifies questions (MCQ=2min, fill=2min, short=5min, essay=8min, scenario=10min, practical=15min), writes CSV report, flags >110% overruns\r\n- tests/test_assessment_timing.py: 8 tests covering all question types, duration calculation, CSV generation, exceeds flagging\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- Lookahead split `(?=^\\s*\\*{0,2}(?:Q|[A-Z])\\d+)` preserves question markers in blocks for accurate classification\r\n- ruff format on this project version is broken (outputs NOT_YET_IMPLEMENTED) — skip it\r\n- Path.is_relative_to() needed for temp file compatibility in tests\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- Previous attempt produced 7061-line diff — kept this to 160 lines by making tool compact\r\n- ruff format destroys Python files in this project — do NOT run it\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  5:55:18 PM\r\nCompleted: Assessment Question Time-Box Validator (ID: US-039) in 7m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 1 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  6:24:04 PM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Tuinalogy Technique Illustration Cross-Reference Indexer (ID: US-055) — 6849 lines > 500 limit — attempt 2/3\r\n\r\n\r\n## Iteration N - Story: WIM Document Readability Analyzer (US-040)\r\n\r\n### What was implemented\r\n- _tools/readability-analyzer.py: analyze_file_readability(), generate_html_report(), CLI entry point\r\n  - textstat FLESCH + Gunning FOG scoring for KP/KT/KK .md files\r\n  - Level detection from path (level-4/, level-5/ → L4/L5, else L3)\r\n  - FLESCH targets: L3>60, L4>65, L5>70\r\n  - CJK text detection (>30% CJK chars) → skips with passes=None (textstat unreliable for Chinese)\r\n  - Generates HTML report to _tools/readability-reports/readability-report.html\r\n  - Problem paragraphs: per-paragraph FLESCH check on paragraphs >80 chars\r\n- tests/test_readability.py: 9 tests — all pass\r\n\r\n### Patterns discovered\r\n- textstat already installed in venv (0.7.13)\r\n- Scanned 321 KP/KT/KK files; 86 CJK (Tuinalogy) skipped gracefully\r\n- importlib.util loading pattern works cleanly for _tools/ scripts\r\n\r\n### Gotchas\r\n- ruff format broken in this project — do NOT run it\r\n- CJK text (Tuinalogy Chinese files) must be detected and skipped; textstat syllable counting is English-only\r\n- _detect_level() checks path parts for level-4 / level-5 folder names\r\n## Iteration 2 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  6:29:55 PM\r\nCompleted: WIM Document Readability Analyzer (ID: US-040) in 4m\r\n\r\n## Iteration 3 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  7:13:36 PM\r\nFAILED diff-guard: Assessment Rubric Standardization and Validator (ID: US-041) — 60107 lines > 500 limit — attempt 1/3\r\n\r\n## Iteration 4 - Fri, Apr 17, 2026  7:18:41 PM\nCompleted: Assessment Rubric Standardization and Validator (ID: US-041) in 4m\n\n\n## Pre-analysis for US-054 (Gemini 2.5 Pro)\n### Technical Brief: US-054 Clinical Vignette Generator\n\n**Objective:** Create a standalone Python CLI tool to generate clinical vignette markdown files for Tuinalogy Competency Units (CUs).\n\n**File Manifest:**\n*   **Primary Target:** `tools/clinical_vignette_generator.py` (New file)\n*   **Test Suite:** `tests/test_vignette_generator.py` (New file)\n*   **Configuration:** `tools/config/vignette-personas.json` (New file)\n*   **Input Data:** `00-noss-extract.md` (Existing file)\n\n**Frappe Context:**\n*   None. This is a standalone Python script and does **not** involve the Frappe framework, DocTypes, or hooks. The initial context mentioning \"lhdn_payroll_integration\" should be disregarded.\n\n**Implementation Plan:**\n1.  Implement `tools/clinical_vignette_generator.py` using Python's `argparse` to handle `--cu` and `--output` arguments.\n2.  The main function will parse `00-noss-extract.md` to find learning outcomes relevant to the specified `cu_code`.\n3.  Load patient persona templates from `tools/config/vignette-personas.json`.\n4.  For the given CU, generate 3-5 unique vignettes by combining personas and learning outcomes.\n5.  Use a markdown template to structure each vignette with the required headers: `患者呈现`, `四诊评估`, `治疗方案`, `预期结果`, `禁忌检查`.\n6.  Write the final markdown content to the specified output path, e.g., `tuinalogy-services/C01/KP(5/N)-clinical-vignettes.md`.\n\n**Gotchas & Edge Cases:**\n*   Ensure the script creates the output directory if it doesn't exist.\n*   Handle errors gracefully if a CU code is not found in the input/c