{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WzJiT2UucLiPTAwR1jYYV9","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Tests for _tools/rubric-standardizer.py (US-041).\n\nRun: uv run pytest tests/test_rubric_standards.py -v\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\n    \"rs\", str(ROOT / \"_tools\" / \"rubric-standardizer.py\")\n)\nassert spec and spec.loader\nrs = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nsys.modules[\"rs\"] = rs\nspec.loader.exec_module(rs)  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n\n\nCOMPLIANT_MD = \"\"\"\\\n# PA — Test CU\n\n| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\n|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\n| Safety | Follows all PPE rules | 10 | Direct observation |\n| Communication | Explains steps clearly | 5 | Verbal check |\n| Technique | Correct procedure | 15 | Checklist |\n\"\"\"\n\nMISSING_EVIDENCE_MD = \"\"\"\\\n# PA — Missing Column\n\n| Criteria | Description | Marks |\n|----------|-------------|-------|\n| Safety | Follows rules | 10 |\n| Technique | Correct | 15 |\n\"\"\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"681cca29-d253-49fb-815d-ba61d351a853","uuid":"b08b5885-b107-430e-a851-035943cbb0d6","timestamp":"2026-04-17T11:22:45.602Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Tests for _tools/rubric-standardizer.py (US-041).\n\nRun: uv run pytest tests/test_rubric_standards.py -v\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\n    \"rs\", str(ROOT / \"_tools\" / \"rubric-standardizer.py\")\n)\nassert spec and spec.loader\nrs = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nsys.modules[\"rs\"] = rs\nspec.loader.exec_module(rs)  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n\n\nCOMPLIANT_MD = \"\"\"\\\n# PA — Test CU\n\n| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\n|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\n| Safety | Follows all PPE rules | 10 | Direct observation |\n| Communication | Explains steps clearly | 5 | Verbal check |\n| Technique | Correct procedure | 15 | Checklist |\n\"\"\"\n\nMISSING_EVIDENCE_MD = \"\"\"\\\n# PA — Missing Column\n\n| Criteria | Description | Marks |\n|----------|-------------|-------|\n| Safety | Follows rules | 10 |\n| Technique | Correct | 15 |\n\"\"\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01CeAjoP57JzSfPYGeFZjUZg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the project. Let me plan the implementation:\n\n1. **`tools/clinical_vignette_generator.py`** - Main CLI tool with:\n   - `generate_vignettes(cu_code, noss_extract_path)` function\n   - Argparse CLI with `--cu` and `--output` \n   - Generates markdown with 3-5 vignettes per CU\n   - Each vignette: 患者呈现, 四诊评估, 治疗方案, 预期结果, 禁忌检查\n   \n2. **`tools/config/vignette-personas.json`** - Patient persona templates for each CU\n\n3. **`tests/test_vignette_generator.py`** - Tests including `test_vignette_structure`\n\nKey constraints:\n- diff limit: ~350 lines\n- ruff format broken in this project — do NOT run it\n- Windows: use encoding='utf-8' for all file ops\n- importlib pattern for loading scripts in tests\n\nFor the personas file, I need to create templates for C01-C05, E01, E02, with each CU having 3-5 personas that vary by age and presentation characteristics.\n\nThe vignettes themselves need to be in simplified Chinese, roughly 150-250 words each, and I'm working out the output path structure. The acceptance criteria specifies `KP(5/N)-clinical-vignettes.md` as a pattern, where N represents the total number of KPs after adding this new one. For C01 which currently has KP-01 through KP-04, this would be KP-05, making N equal to 5.\n\nI should probably have the tool dynamically determine N based on existing KP files in the folder, though for now I could use a fixed value. As for the file size constraints, I need to keep the tool compact and focused on the essentials—loading personas from the config JSON, generating the vignettes based on those personas, and writing them to the correct location.\n\nI'm planning to split this across three files: the generator script itself at around 100 lines, a JSON config file with persona data for all 7 CUs at roughly 100 lines, and a test file at about 60 lines. That keeps me well under the 350-line budget. Since the vignettes need to be 150-250 words in Chinese, I'll use templates with the persona data injected directly from the config rather than generating them dynamically.\n\nThe most practical approach is to store the vignette content pre-written in the JSON config file alongside the persona information, then have the tool read the NOSS extract to pull out the CU name and key topics, combine that with the persona templates, and format everything into the correct markdown structure. I'm weighing the tradeoffs between storing pre-written vignettes in JSON versus generating them dynamically with templates. Pre-written content keeps the Python simple and ensures quality Chinese text, but I need to verify it fits the 150-250 word requirement per vignette.\n\nThe word count is ambiguous for Chinese—it could mean characters or words. I'll interpret it as 150-250 total Chinese characters per vignette across all 5 sections, which is actually quite compact. Given that constraint, a template-based approach makes more sense: I'll store persona data (age, gender, condition, symptoms) in JSON and use Python to assemble the 5 sections from templates with 1-3 sentences each.\n\nNow I'm planning the content structure for the 7 clinical use cases, starting with C01 for consultation services.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":448,"cache_read_input_tokens":35177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":448},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"681cca29-d253-49fb-815d-ba61d351a853","uuid":"004f7700-6164-40c5-a713-e37fe6aa1db9"}
