{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018T75PBn8QMc8N8gtUbHWUv","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Tests for _tools/readability-analyzer.py (US-040).\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\n    \"ra\", str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"_tools\" / \"readability-analyzer.py\")\n)\nassert spec and spec.loader\nra = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nsys.modules[\"ra\"] = ra\nspec.loader.exec_module(ra)  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n\n# Simple high-FLESCH English text (short words, short sentences)\nEASY_TEXT = (\n    \"The cat sat on the mat. The dog ran fast. It was a good day. \"\n    \"Sun is bright. Kids play well. She can run and jump far. \"\n    \"He read the book. We like to learn new things each day. \"\n) * 8\n\n# Complex low-FLESCH text (long multi-syllable words, long sentences)\nHARD_TEXT = (\n    \"The electrocardiographic manifestations of ventricular hypertrophy demonstrate \"\n    \"characteristic morphological alterations in the precordial and limb lead configurations, \"\n    \"necessitating comprehensive electrophysiological interpretation methodologies \"\n    \"for accurate cardiovascular pathophysiological assessment.\"\n) * 6","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"681cca29-d253-49fb-815d-ba61d351a853","uuid":"8264f658-6fa1-4965-a9d9-ebaddab51d2c","timestamp":"2026-04-17T11:23:45.531Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Tests for _tools/readability-analyzer.py (US-040).\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\n    \"ra\", str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"_tools\" / \"readability-analyzer.py\")\n)\nassert spec and spec.loader\nra = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nsys.modules[\"ra\"] = ra\nspec.loader.exec_module(ra)  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n\n# Simple high-FLESCH English text (short words, short sentences)\nEASY_TEXT = (\n    \"The cat sat on the mat. The dog ran fast. It was a good day. \"\n    \"Sun is bright. Kids play well. She can run and jump far. \"\n    \"He read the book. We like to learn new things each day. \"\n) * 8\n\n# Complex low-FLESCH text (long multi-syllable words, long sentences)\nHARD_TEXT = (\n    \"The electrocardiographic manifestations of ventricular hypertrophy demonstrate \"\n    \"characteristic morphological alterations in the precordial and limb lead configurations, \"\n    \"necessitating comprehensive electrophysiological interpretation methodologies \"\n    \"for accurate cardiovascular pathophysiological assessment.\"\n) * 6","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01EGet8AitHiX98N8QuQj51x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the patterns. Let me plan my implementation:\n\n**Phase 1: Plan**\n\nFiles to create:\n1. `tools/config/vignette-personas.json` - Patient persona data for all 7 CUs\n2. `tools/clinical_vignette_generator.py` - CLI tool + generate_vignettes() function\n3. `tests/test_vignette_generator.py` - Tests with test_vignette_structure\n\n**File size budget:**\n- Python tool: ~90 lines\n- JSON config: ~100 lines (compact, no full vignette text - just persona data)\n\n\n- Test file: ~60 lines\n- Total: ~250 lines\n\n**Design approach:**\n- JSON config stores CU info and persona templates (age, gender, condition, chief_complaint)  \n- Python tool generates Chinese vignette sections using template strings filled with persona data\n- Sections are template-driven so the code is compact\n\n**CU-specific conditions:**\n- C01 (咨询 Consultation): 颈肩痛, 腰痛, 头痛 etc. - focus on intake/assessment\n- C02 (全身推拿 Full Body): 全身疲劳, 压力/失眠, 亚健康\n- C03 (运动推拿 Sport): 运动损伤 - each CU has distinct clinical scenarios and assessment priorities\n- C04 (肌肉骨骼 Musculoskeletal): 颈椎病, 腰椎间盘, 肩周炎\n- C05 (行政管理 Administration): case/record management focus\n- E01 (小儿推拿 Paediatric): 小儿感冒, 厌食, 便秘, 腹泻\n- E02 (妇女推拿 Women): 痛经, 产后调理, 更年期症状\n\n**Vignette template structure:**\nBuilding out the vignette format with patient presentation, four-exam assessment...\n\nI'm thinking about the JSON structure to store these vignettes efficiently. Rather than embedding full markdown, I'll organize the content by clinical unit and persona, with each vignette containing the key sections: title, presentation, assessment, treatment, outcome, and contraindication checks. This way the Python script just reads the JSON and formats it into markdown, keeping the code minimal while housing all the rich Chinese medical content in a structured format.\n\nFor the implementation strategy, I need to balance file size against the 350-line diff limit. I'll create a compact JSON file with just the essential persona data—ID, name, age, gender, chief complaint—and let Python templates generate the clinical sections based on the CU type. This keeps the JSON lean while the generator handles the text generation logic.\n\nWriting the clinical vignette generator... Generating clinical vignettes... I need to finish setting up the main function - normalizing the CU code, creating the output directory, checking for existing KP files to determine the next sequence number, and then writing the generated vignettes to a markdown file with proper naming.\n\nWait, I'm realizing the acceptance criteria specifies a different filename format - it should be `KP(5/N)-clinical-vignettes.md` where the number represents the current KP and N is the total count, not the zero-padded format I was using. Let me reconsider what N should be - for a CU with existing KP-01 through KP-04, the next file would be KP-05, making it `KP(5/5)-clinical-vignettes.md`. The N value depends on how many total KPs that particular CU will have, which I need to figure out from the existing files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":38102,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":455},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"681cca29-d253-49fb-815d-ba61d351a853","uuid":"eb4a6afd-4f92-401a-88f2-f90cb3750365"}
